<section class="section legal-page">

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>This website — berlindisch.co — is a static informational and editorial site operated by Berlindisch, an informal cultural and media collective based in Berlin, Germany.</p>
  <p>We take privacy seriously and have deliberately designed this site to minimize data collection. This privacy policy explains how personal data is handled in accordance with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the German Federal Data Protection Act (BDSG), and the German Telecommunications-Telemedia Data Protection Act (TTDSG).</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Responsible Party</h2>
  <p>The party responsible for data processing on this website within the meaning of the GDPR is:</p>
  <p><strong>Berlindisch</strong><br>Berlin, Germany<br>Email: <a href="mailto:ahoi@berlindisch.co">ahoi@berlindisch.co</a></p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Cookies &amp; Tracking (TTDSG)</h2>
  <p>This site currently does not intentionally use tracking or advertising cookies. Pursuant to § 25 TTDSG (Telekommunikation-Telemedien-Datenschutz-Gesetz), no consent-requiring cookies or similar technologies are stored on or read from your device when you visit this site.</p>
  <p>Specifically, this site does not:</p>
  <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: 0.75rem;">
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>use analytics tools (no Google Analytics, Plausible, Matomo, or similar)</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>set tracking or marketing cookies</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>use advertising or retargeting pixels</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>embed third-party social media widgets or trackers</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>load external fonts or scripts from third-party servers</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>collect personal data through forms or user accounts</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">Because no cookies or equivalent storage technologies are used, a cookie consent banner is not required for this site.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Hosting &amp; Server Logs</h2>
  <p>This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. When you visit, the hosting provider may automatically collect and store technical information in server logs, including:</p>
  <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: 0.75rem;">
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>your IP address</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>browser type and version</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>date and time of access</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>pages visited</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">This data is collected by the hosting infrastructure, not by us. We do not have direct access to these logs. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in the secure and reliable operation of the website). For more information, see <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub's Privacy Statement</a>.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Email Contact</h2>
  <p>This site provides contact via <code>mailto:</code> links. If you send us an email, you voluntarily share your email address and message content with us. We process this data solely to respond to your inquiry. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in responding to inquiries). We will not share this information with third parties.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Social Media Presences</h2>
  <p>This site contains links to our social media profiles on Instagram, X (formerly Twitter), and Mastodon. These are simple outbound links and do not embed third-party content or transmit data to those platforms when you visit this site. Data processing by those platforms occurs only if you choose to follow the links and visit the respective platform, subject to their own privacy policies.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">External Links</h2>
  <p>This site may contain links to external websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of those sites. We recommend reviewing their privacy policies independently.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Your Rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR (Articles 15–21) and the BDSG, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
  <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: 0.75rem;">
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>Right of access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>Right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>Right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>Right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>Right to object (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
    <li style="color: var(--color-muted); padding: 0.2rem 0;"><span style="color: var(--color-rose);">→ </span>Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR)</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">Given the minimal data footprint of this site, most of these rights are unlikely to apply in practice. The competent supervisory authority is the Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit.</p>
  <p>If you have questions or concerns, contact us at <a href="mailto:ahoi@berlindisch.co">ahoi@berlindisch.co</a>.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>This policy may evolve as the Berlindisch collective grows and its activities expand. Any significant changes will be reflected on this page.</p>

  <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-surface); margin: 2rem 0;">
